The coefficient of determination, denoted as $R^2$ , is a statistical measure that indicates how well the data fits a regression model. In this context, $\Delta AP_{lh}^{\mathrm{complex}}$ represents the observed change in activation patterns at layer $l$ and head $h$ for a complex task, while $\Delta \hat{AP}_{lh}^{\mathrm{complex}}$ denotes the corresponding predicted change. The numerator captures the sum of squared errors between the observed and predicted values, whereas the denominator reflects the total variance in the observed data. $\overline{\Delta AP^{\mathrm{complex}}}$ represents the mean of the observed changes in activation patterns.
